designs.docModel:
New KIND `text` added to document/model.mjs KINDS + KEY (`texts`), SELECTABLE (yes — it is a placed, selectable entity like node/zone). Doc shape (px center-origin, mirroring node, plus an integer cell span):
  { id:'text-ab12cd', kind:'text',
    role:'label'|'button'|'input'|'bar',   // discriminator; default 'label'
    x, y,                                   // px center of the TOP-LEFT cell of the run (the anchor cell-centre)
    cols, rows,                             // integer cell span ≥1 (rows for multi-line/backplanes)
    text,                                   // displayed string (the label/title/button caption)
    value,                                  // input role only: the editable slot contents
    align }                                 // 'center'|'left'; role default (label/button=center, input=left)
Factory:
  makeText(text, pos, role='label') {
    return { id:newId('text'), role, x:pos.x, y:pos.y, ...spanFor(text, role), text, value:'' };
  }
  // spanFor measures text px (reuse pillWidth's 9px-ASCII/15px-CJK metric) then QUANTIZES to whole cells:
  // cols = max(1, ceil((textPx + 2*HPAD + 20) / P)), rows=1.  (input adds slot width; bar is sized by host.)
makeButton/makeInput/makeBar are thin wrappers over makeText with the role preset (and value for input). The model stays pure (no DOM); cascade/occupancy lives in commands.js.

node grows a discriminated `content` plus per-variant payload and an optional `span`:
  glyph  (default): { id, name, type, shape, x, y }                         // unchanged; content omitted ⇒ 'glyph'
  text :  { id, content:'text',   text:"Diagram title", shape:'none', x, y, span:{cols,rows} }
  button: { id, content:'button', text:"Export",        shape:'square', x, y, span }
  input:  { id, content:'input',  label:"Name:", value:"web-tier", shape:'square', x, y, span }
  panel:  { id, content:'panel',  shape:'square', x, y, span:{cols:6,rows:2} }   // a host plane; widgets are separate nodes grouped to it
Factories live next to makeNode in document/model.mjs, all returning the SAME id-namespace ('node-xxxxxx'): makeText(text,pos,span), makeButton(text,pos), makeInput(label,value,pos,span), makePanel(pos,span). `content` joins `shape` in the OPTIONAL set so absence ⇒ 'glyph'; `text`/`label`/`value` are str(…,N)-bounded, `span` is {cols,rows} clamped ≥1. `type` is no longer required for non-glyph content (its field validator becomes content-conditional). Critically nothing else in the KINDS list, the KEY map, SELECTABLE, or toJSON/load changes — text/button/input round-trip as nodes.
